      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "When the Pennsylvania Railroad laid tracks through Third Street in 1849, Newport instantly became a bustling railroad hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Newport%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "By 1905 the PRR had moved its tracks onto the old towpath, a new roadbed that still traces the canal’s path today.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.nrps-pa.org/welcome-to-newport/history-of-newport/",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Newport’s historic district and the nearby Bridge in Newport Borough are listed on the National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Newport%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The town’s playground and youth baseball fields now occupy the site of a 19th‑century tannery that operated until the early 20th century.",
